K-Means:

---> For grouping or forming clusters.
---> We will decide the number of clusters that is needed.
---> Cluster value needs to be in odd number for overcome bias
---> Number of Cluster formation is subjective to the specific issue or dataset
---> UnSupervised Learning.

Formation:

1. give the n_clusters = 3.
1.1 means, initially or randomly we groups the entire dataset into
    3 clusters. because i have given 3 in the number
1.2 Each cluster will be assigned a "Centroids" randomly
1.3 Now based on the centroids , distance will be calculated,
then datapoint which is near by to that will be forming group.
1.4 once done, new centroids will be formed, and then same process
will happen until entire groups are grouped or clustered.

Note: Movement or change of centroids is based mean of those datapoint.

